WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:58.051 --> 00:00:59.366
Hello everyone,

00:00:59.366 --> 00:01:00.466
I'm Hiker CP. We're currently in

00:01:00.466 --> 00:01:01.500
The Pass in the Middle—The

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:02.700
Pass in the Middle, huh?

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.600
A spot for climbing

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:05.833
Mount Kuhanosin

00:01:05.833 --> 00:01:09.200
The last time I visited Zhongzhiguan,
I think I hiked the Southern Section 1.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.900
The southern section
goes up from here.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:14.333
I’m a bit confused—I took
the charcoal kiln path.

00:01:14.333 --> 00:01:17.433
I drove alone on the South Hengshan
Highway on Monday; there

00:01:17.433 --> 00:01:20.666
was no traffic jam at the Meishan
Checkpoint just now.

00:01:20.666 --> 00:01:22.266
I can't get in until 7:00.

00:01:22.266 --> 00:01:25.066
I'm getting closer to my goal
of climbing 100 peaks!

00:01:25.066 --> 00:01:28.133
I've been wanting to complete
the 100 for a while now,

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:31.333
but I'm stuck at 92. It's the easiest one,
but the hardest to drive.

00:01:31.333 --> 00:01:32.666
Two
-Star Hike on the Southern Cross-Island

00:01:32.666 --> 00:01:34.600
Highway: Taguan Mountain
&amp; Guanshan Ridge

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:37.433
Depart Kaohsiung at 5:00 a.m.,

00:01:37.433 --> 00:01:40.600
arrive in Meishan at 7:00 a.m., and are scheduled to
arrive at the Taguan Mountain trailhead at 8:00 a.m.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.766
Let's save the small
talk for later (??).

00:01:42.766 --> 00:01:46.000
Let's keep driving toward
Taguan Mountain, guys!

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.966
We can now see the Southern Section
1 of the Great Trail coming

00:01:47.966 --> 00:01:51.900
down from this side,
and then heading up to Southern Section 1.

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:53.566
Arrival at the Kuhanosin Mountain
Hut—Twelfth Night,

00:01:53.566 --> 00:01:55.533
Kuhanosin

00:01:55.533 --> 00:01:56.600
After walking a bit further south,

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:00.566
they headed straight for
Kuhanosin like this.

00:02:00.566 --> 00:02:04.866
I'm totally exhausted after hiking this far on the Great Trail.
There's a stream here where I can get water.

00:02:04.866 --> 00:02:09.233
My older brother said the weather would change this afternoon,
so we should head to Taguan Mountain first.

00:02:09.233 --> 00:02:13.760
The view is better from there. If the view is good,
check it out first, then head to Guanshan Ridge—otherwise, there’s no view.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:14.800
It's okay if it gets foggy.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.340
He just mentioned that
he watched my video.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.260
I only started hiking last year—check
out my videos to learn about

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:19.980
day hikes and the "100 Peaks" challenge.
We’re not here to...

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:21.880
What's there to brag about? We just want
to share some hiking information.

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:24.180
Here's an update on the trail conditions
to help everyone hike more safely.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:25.820
That's just...

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:26.800
Empty talk is just empty talk.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:27.980
Keep driving and...

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:29.266
It hasn't even opened

00:02:29.266 --> 00:02:30.680
yet! Bonfus 23L

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:32.666
It works really,

00:02:35.735 --> 00:02:36.909
really well. The battery's dead XD

00:02:42.849 --> 00:02:44.678
Bring two packs of pectin each time.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.590
Get ready to go—short
sleeves and shorts.

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:53.430
As for Mount Taguan, it’s one of the Three
Sacred Mountains of the Central Peak.

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:55.550
The one in the middle—it’s
actually called Daguanshan,

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:57.450
which was its original name.

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:59.070
It's easy to confuse Daguanshan and Guanshan,
just like

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:01.050
I would never confuse Xueshan
with Daxueshan,

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:03.090
but just to be sure I don’t mix them up,
that’s why I...

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:05.350
It’s now called Taguan Mountain,

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:08.785
so Daguanshan must have been the old name.
The view from there is fantastic.

00:03:09.933 --> 00:03:11.190
I'm currently walking along the South Cross
-Island Highway; I'm at the 33.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.954
3k mark right now.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.470
I don't know why,

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:17.890
but I'm feeling a little excited and a little out
of breath. We're already at an elevation of 2,500

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:20.210
Then, once it hits 3,
200, it’ll go up quite a bit.

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:22.670
The Three Mountains of the Nanheng
Highway—so let's park

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:24.950
at the parking lot up ahead.
It should be about...

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:26.730
It's only 3–400 meters, so the open space
there is pretty big (about 10 cars).

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:28.370
You probably shouldn't drive
all the way to the trailhead.

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:29.790
I'm explaining this in such detail
because it's my first time here.

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:31.250
That's why it can be confusing.

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:33.030
I've heard that Taguan Mountain
offers a better view.

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:35.870
I've noticed some strange
things happening lately.

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:37.610
My new friend asked me why
I keep saying “doggie.”

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:39.890
What is a dog? What is
a dog? A dog is...

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:42.190
We want the dog to go—call the dog,
Doggie! (XDDD)

00:03:48.354 --> 00:03:49.527
Trailhead: This time,

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:53.630
I’m using this Long Peak 9+

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:56.030
Since I have some work to do this time,
I’m going to...

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:57.630
I'm too lazy to bring an extra pair of shoes,
so I just use

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:00.010
Long Peak 9+—So let's
go hike it today.

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:01.550
Hiking—Actually,

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:03.590
I haven’t actually taken them on any of the “100 Peaks,
” but they’re trail running shoes, and...

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:05.790
It's very light and comfortable,

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:08.070
so I'm confident this terrain and difficulty
level won't be a problem. OK, great.

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:11.350
We're now at the trailhead for Mount
Taguan—all set for Mount Taguan.

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:13.570
Actually, you can connect here...

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:15.209
In the southern section—I just mentioned
Kuhanoshin and Taguan Mountain,

00:04:15.209 --> 00:04:17.430
and then there’s Guanshan Ridge—

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:19.829
That's all for now.
Before setting off,

00:04:19.829 --> 00:04:22.570
we were worried about not getting enough sleep,
so we opted for O2 capsules.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:24.770
Increasing oxygen levels is
helpful for acclimatization

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:28.410
at high altitudes; you can
roughly estimate this.

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:30.150
Because the mountain
climb is very long,

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:31.570
unlike a race where you need to be precise,
you might need to plan ahead before the race.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:33.890
You have 60 to 90 minutes to eat,

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:35.930
but if you're hiking, you'll have
to get to the trailhead or your morning...

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:38.690
It's fine to eat it after getting
up and during your commute,

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:41.142
as it can last for 6 hours.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:45.250
There was a bear sighting
last October,

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:47.770
and this bear was...

00:04:47.770 --> 00:04:49.900
This looks okay, looks good.

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:54.390
Let's

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:56.610
go first!

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:59.066
Let's see what we can
see on the way, dog!

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:15.740
At an altitude of 2600 meters,

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:16.800
I was very breathless and slept very little,
waking up early most of the time.

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:27.833
The garrison station,

00:05:34.536 --> 00:05:35.900
where many Japanese troops were stationed, was also located along the Southern Cross
-Island Highway.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:38.400
The roads around the ruins
from that period

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:42.940
are well paved; I haven't
seen any yet.

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:45.380
A strip of cloth clearly
indicates the path.

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:46.066
That's already

00:05:52.333 --> 00:05:53.880
one
-third complete.

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:55.860
One
-third done? (Super fast!) Quite a few shuttle buses came today.

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:58.140
So I won't be lonely today
since I'm hiking.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:05:59.633
Lonely in the Northern
Hemisphere (so old...).

00:05:59.633 --> 00:06:01.040
They all look like retired seniors.

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:04.080
Who would go on Monday?

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:07.200
Among those climbing
to two stars here,

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:10.460
besides myself, I'm probably the only one who
hasn't retired and is still working hard.

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:11.633
Eating an energy bar like

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:30.266
this will make you hungry.

00:06:35.766 --> 00:06:37.400
This mountain is so
accessible; as long

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:39.620
as you have good driving skills...

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:43.300
You don't need to be a
great climber to come here.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:48.393
Cedarwood,

00:06:48.393 --> 00:06:49.323
wow~

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:51.080
Many retirees thought they

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:53.339
had come to Qixing Mountain

00:06:53.339 --> 00:06:54.760
(The first day was Guanshanling)

00:07:00.988 --> 00:07:02.640
This group had some...

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:04.500
The young people and their elders originally
traveled in tour groups,

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:07.060
so they essentially carpooled
between different locations.

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:08.066
Wow, this is so cool! I didn't

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.920
know there was such a schedule.

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:13.660
Therefore, it's uncertain whether
they lived there or not.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:15.640
It's really strange that they only give out one coin a day on the Southern Cross
-Island

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:17.560
Highway. Where should we stay here then?
That would be quite interesting.

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:19.660
But that makes things much easier.
We see now...

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:22.980
This should be the Cloud

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:23.600
Shirt Iron Shirt.

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:25.680
I think this pointed shape is
like Eagle's Beak Mountain

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:27.920
or Dinosaur Point Mountain;
it's a huge cliff.

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:29.920
If you really want to hike the
Central Mountain Range without

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:32.247
leaving the highway,
this section is extremely dangerous.

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:33.380
Chixin Peak and his team originally
planned to scout ahead,

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:35.720
but they needed to set up ropes.

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:37.640
Ensuring a delay would be too risky,

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:40.500
so that's not the approach
we've taken.

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:41.760
I didn't leave then either.

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:44.360
There's a place called (Xitou Mountain) near Guanshanling,
I remember.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:46.320
It was a very memorable experience
when I came out of the trailhead,

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:48.740
headfirst and feet stuck
in some reeds.

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:50.260
It's a pity I couldn't take a picture
because it was right next to the road.

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:53.200
Because I was already close
to dying at that point,

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.520
and then I was even more exhausted that day,
which is what I just described.

00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:57.720
As far as I can remember,

00:07:57.720 --> 00:07:59.260
climbing those four thousand steps at Cuhannosin
took me the whole afternoon.

00:07:59.260 --> 00:08:01.500
That staircase on the buttocks
was very tiring to walk on.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:03.440
It was a difficult time; it was already
the twelfth day when I saw this.

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:08.340
This should be...

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:10.480
It should be the southern
section of the road;

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:11.600
below is the Southern Cross
-Island Highway.

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:12.360
Let me just talk about these
Long Peak 9+ shoes.

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:14.020
I usually use them as...

00:08:14.020 --> 00:08:17.140
These are everyday shoes,

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:19.540
but they're really versatile. Perfect for casual
hiking in the suburbs or giving a speech in Tainan XD

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:23.180
No problem at all,

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:25.540
because these are trail running shoes with zero drop and zero foot difference,
they're very comfortable.

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:27.200
It feels like barefoot,
but it also has a layer of sole.

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:29.480
It has a gold
-plated outsole,

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:33.440
so it's slip
-resistant. The road is very dry today, so it should be...

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:34.633
I'm not very good at skating
and I've already gone 1.

00:08:36.405 --> 00:08:37.908
3 meters.

00:08:37.966 --> 00:08:40.000
There's less than
a kilometer left,

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:42.700
so there should be a section that's a cliff,
because that's the cliff of Guanshan (right?).

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:45.020
This mountain also has some cliffs,

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:49.000
and I'm still getting used to the high altitude,
but I'm almost there now.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.780
I'm a bit out of breath about 3,

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:53.880
000 because I've been driving for more
than three hours since this morning.

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:55.760
I slept a little less yesterday.
We have money and free time,

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:58.720
no need to show off.
We have money and free time...

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:02.140
Participating in the three
-day Southern Cross-Island Highway 3-star tour will be very

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:04.640
comfortable, OK? If you're short on time,
make sure you're physically fit.

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:06.233
It's no problem to attack alone;
you've completely misunderstood.

00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:24.560
The person behind this
is Guanshanbei.

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:27.780
So what you see over there is
the (Kuhanosing) mountain hut.

00:09:27.892 --> 00:09:30.600
Guanshan North (Guanshan is behind)
and then you can walk from here.

00:09:30.631 --> 00:09:33.860
Yingzaizui Mountain is like this, and then the Southern Cross
-Island Highway is below.

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:34.466
Here are zpacks

00:09:44.173 --> 00:09:45.233
backpacks

00:09:55.766 --> 00:09:56.939
(This is the cliff
terrain on the map)

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:09.190
We've basically passed the cliff.

00:10:09.190 --> 00:10:11.810
More dangerous than Wuliaojian
when you're bored?

00:10:11.810 --> 00:10:13.650
If you've been to Wuliaojian,
you don't need to worry about anything.

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:15.810
The cliff at Taguan Mountain
isn't actually a cliff,

00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:18.690
and there are nets laid out there; fast people
should be able to finish in about an hour.

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:21.404
You can go up now, it's about 58 minutes past the hour,
climbing 1.8k.

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:24.730
There are 400 meters left. If I run,

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:25.466
I could probably reach the
summit in 40 minutes.

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:47.850
You can go, but you need to drive
to Yingzaizui or Guanshan North.

00:10:48.350 --> 00:10:50.610
Behind Guanshan is the southern
section of Yingzaizui

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:56.970
Mountain and Dinosaur Tower,
past Guanshan North.

00:10:56.970 --> 00:11:00.090
It should be Guanshan,

00:11:01.250 --> 00:11:04.633
and then this is the mountain hut,
which should be Cuhanosin.

00:11:04.633 --> 00:11:05.270
Jade Mountain,

00:11:05.270 --> 00:11:08.690
this is Jade Mountain,
it's clearly concave.

00:11:08.690 --> 00:11:11.250
From Xiangyang Mountain,

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:15.330
turn right at the 7K mark (downhill from
Jiaming Lake Trail) to Xitou Mountain.

00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:17.270
But I had already descended
Xitou Mountain by then.

00:11:17.270 --> 00:11:19.470
Reaching Guanshanling brings
up the question of why

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:21.950
I haven't been there before;
I should have gone.

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:24.000
Guanshanling seems to be relatively

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:25.790
easy to walk down.

00:11:28.566 --> 00:11:29.666
(Passing through) Mobolai Mountain

00:11:33.693 --> 00:11:36.240
and Blakesan Mountain

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:39.327
Then there's the southern
ridge of Mount

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:42.066
Bracksan XXX I forgot the location.

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:16.840
After you come up on the map,
turn left and there will be a road.

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:20.680
You can go directly down to the Southern Cross
-Island Highway;

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:22.600
there should be a highway
here that leads down.

00:12:34.530 --> 00:12:37.810
I didn't take any electrolyte supplements before going up the mountain,
so I'll take a packet of dried plums (400mg electrolytes) first.

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:40.050
There's a very,

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:43.350
very clear path leading here, but this area is very fragmented,
and information online...

00:12:43.350 --> 00:12:45.210
They all need to untie the ropes
because the ropes over there

00:12:45.210 --> 00:12:47.950
are quite weak,
and there's nowhere to set them up.

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:51.330
Usually, people say there's nowhere to put it,
or even...

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:52.790
Unstable terrain usually
presents two types of

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:54.970
terrain: one is to walk
through the middle.

00:12:54.970 --> 00:12:57.210
The other one at the very top is
to wrap it around your waist.

00:12:57.210 --> 00:13:00.150
But both are extremely
difficult to navigate,

00:13:00.150 --> 00:13:01.200
and the description is terrifying.

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:02.830
That's right (right

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:10.700
what??) This time use

00:13:12.433 --> 00:13:14.520
This action camera,

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:17.620
the latest photography camera,
has zoom (slip of the tongue, aperture).

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:19.818
It has a variable aperture of F2.0
-F4.0,

00:13:19.866 --> 00:13:21.180
so it is a variable aperture.

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:22.900
This is its latest feature,

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:24.866
featuring dual front
and rear cameras.

00:13:24.866 --> 00:13:26.200
It's very clear,

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:29.020
the colors are very vibrant,
I think it's quite cool.

00:13:29.020 --> 00:13:31.620
The original tripod is
actually quite light

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:34.800
and can be extended to
a fairly long length.

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:37.560
The neutral density filter is currently
used for strong sunlight exposure,

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:41.420
so it also has an 8/16/32 setting.

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:43.800
The larger the number,

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:47.260
the more light it blocks.
This makes it clearer how much light it blocks.

00:13:53.090 --> 00:13:55.890
If you don't want to reduce
the color too much,

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:58.700
then this is a lighter shade.

00:13:59.930 --> 00:14:01.750
It has the feel of a camera,

00:14:01.750 --> 00:14:04.590
and the image sensor is very large,
so its...

00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:07.610
The colors are very clear,
so what you see now is the actual photo.

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:11.070
The resulting image,

00:14:11.933 --> 00:14:14.870
resembling a sunny mountain, also has excellent anti
-shake performance.

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:16.990
Because of this aperture,
you can take photos at night.

00:14:16.990 --> 00:14:19.930
Shooting in relatively dark woods generally
results in brighter images.

00:14:19.930 --> 00:14:22.290
I used to shoot in the woods.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.250
It can actually be quite dark,
especially in the evening.

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:25.970
It's not very usable because
of the image sensor,

00:14:25.970 --> 00:14:28.010
which makes it more...

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:30.350
It's more convenient,

00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:32.450
and the device itself is waterproof, which is actually
an advantage even though I don't go underwater.

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:34.370
But if it rains while hiking,
waterproofing is...

00:14:34.370 --> 00:14:36.210
A major advantage is that it
has a barebones version.

00:14:36.210 --> 00:14:36.774
It's about 20 meters underwater,

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:26.660
past that collapsed wall,
there's a net here...

00:15:26.660 --> 00:15:28.320
The happy descent from the mountain
just now was to say that Taguan

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:31.560
Mountain is my 93rd mountain.
We really started from 92.

00:15:32.130 --> 00:15:34.140
Progress reached 93,

00:15:34.140 --> 00:15:36.800
then stagnated for two years, right? Add one,
wait, it'll be two more this year, but will it happen this year?

00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:38.533
Going to Marburg is still uncertain,

00:15:38.586 --> 00:15:40.620
just because the elders don't know me very well,
and then there's a...

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:42.066
The young man,

00:15:42.066 --> 00:15:44.839
recognizing me, said: "You've finally gotten rid of XX." (His words were too explicit,
so I'll refer to it as "commonplace matters.")

00:15:44.899 --> 00:15:46.160
Please don't misunderstand or mislead
me. I didn't think that way,

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:49.440
okay? Anyway, that's all.

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:53.966
Do our thing,

00:16:07.490 --> 00:16:10.030
climb our mountain, OK? A recent news story is about Nims,
who filmed...

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:12.430
Netflix's fastest person to complete 14 8000
-meter altitude climbs without oxygen

00:16:12.430 --> 00:16:15.230
An avalanche could wipe
out the entire team;

00:16:15.230 --> 00:16:18.850
such things just happen all the time.

00:16:18.850 --> 00:16:21.010
I'm a little unsure how to
express risk and probability.

00:16:21.010 --> 00:16:23.710
It expresses my thoughts
and emotions.

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:25.550
There is a chance that
it will happen, so we

00:16:25.550 --> 00:16:27.190
We must accept it and face it,

00:16:27.190 --> 00:16:29.450
but I believe that those with a lot
of experience are not necessarily...

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:31.290
I think anyone who can climb 8000
meters is basically someone

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:33.330
who has climbed all 100 highest
peaks in the world.

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:35.930
Everyone imagines encountering various
problems on the mountain,

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:39.050
and if things aren't handled well,
they might indeed end up stuck there.

00:16:39.050 --> 00:16:41.470
I've actually thought about this quite a lot,
but we need to...

00:16:41.470 --> 00:16:42.341
What we're doing is reducing

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:43.500
the probability of this.

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:45.830
Why do we keep promoting
mountaineering?

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:48.290
Safety education,

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:50.370
mountaineering knowledge, experience,
equipment, route planning, and physical training.

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:52.570
These are all factors that greatly
reduce the impact of this matter,

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:55.030
so put yourself in the
shoes of others.

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:57.610
I was getting ready to go up the mountain
again when I met that guy

00:16:57.610 --> 00:16:59.390
at Kuhanoshin on the southern section;
it was quite touching.

00:16:59.390 --> 00:17:01.550
He said I wasn't just showing
off how fast I walk.

00:17:01.550 --> 00:17:04.290
The route video,

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:06.770
experience and knowledge sharing, and the equipment
were really helpful; he wanted to do his homework.

00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:09.569
The main purpose I want
to convey in my video

00:17:09.569 --> 00:17:12.271
is to launch a solo attack on Yushan.

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:15.310
The purpose was to take these pictures
for everyone's reference,

00:17:15.310 --> 00:17:17.770
so the guy just now had no idea...

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:19.750
Going up to the river,

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:22.430
to study the river,
to plan his route and time.

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:24.950
I think this is truly a very,
very rare thing.

00:17:24.950 --> 00:17:27.250
I hope everyone can have a happy climb
up the mountain and a safe descent.

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:30.550
This is probably the core
thing I do for this

00:17:30.550 --> 00:17:33.110
show; I've been
on it for too long.

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:35.070
Before returning to Guanshan,

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:37.250
when collecting the Hundred Peaks,
quickly go and pick up that one (Guanshan Ridge).

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:41.050
You can happily rest
and suddenly feel

00:17:41.050 --> 00:17:42.950
My mood became very cheerful; it seemed like
I had just started climbing the mountain.

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:45.910
I don't feel that happy yet,
but I think it might be.

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:48.510
After chatting with
those fellow hikers,

00:17:48.510 --> 00:17:50.690
I felt a sudden change in my mood.

00:17:50.690 --> 00:17:51.299
It's nice to wear a STATIC

00:17:51.299 --> 00:17:53.210
short
-sleeved shirt today.

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:55.970
He used this kind of interlaced
(undulating) material

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:57.890
Some parts are close to the skin,

00:17:57.890 --> 00:17:59.830
while others are not,
allowing for faster heat dissipation.

00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:01.370
Half wool (50% wool) is perfect for single
-target attacks.

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:02.990
For a two
-day trip or a longer trip,

00:18:02.990 --> 00:18:05.550
I might use all
-wool, which is very...

00:18:05.550 --> 00:18:07.690
It dries quickly and feels cool; today it's
probably around 20 degrees Celsius.

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:09.610
It might be a little cold if you sit

00:18:09.610 --> 00:18:11.330
down to rest; it still has some wool.

00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:12.910
It has excellent warmth retention,

00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:15.270
wicks away sweat quickly,
and doesn't stick to the body during the process.

00:18:15.270 --> 00:18:16.550
Pure wool does feel quite
clingy to the body,

00:18:16.550 --> 00:18:20.210
but it's only 50% wool,
so it's very sheer and flowy.

00:18:20.210 --> 00:18:21.750
I'd like to recommend
a Japanese brand called...

00:18:21.750 --> 00:18:23.570
Static has previously mentioned having
hundreds of stores in Japan,

00:18:23.570 --> 00:18:26.030
but it seems they only
have one in Taiwan.

00:18:26.030 --> 00:18:27.870
More and more materials
are being released,

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:30.230
so everyone can try them out; they're not expensive,
just over two thousand yuan.

00:18:30.230 --> 00:18:32.270
A high
-end brand pure wool item costing three or four thousand

00:18:32.270 --> 00:18:33.850
is a pretty good option compared
to other brands.

00:18:33.850 --> 00:18:36.694
Okay, we can see the Evergreen
Shrine halfway down.

00:18:36.733 --> 00:18:39.730
OSMO Action 6 is truly very stable.

00:18:39.730 --> 00:18:42.870
The fact that my legs are wobbling
like this is because

00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:46.770
of its shock absorption; it's
extremely stable.

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:52.666
The stability is excellent,

00:18:52.666 --> 00:18:53.390
and because it is mainly...

00:18:53.390 --> 00:18:54.990
I think very vibrant colors
are what I would want.

00:18:54.990 --> 00:18:57.370
Its horizontal cut can also
be directly cut vertically.

00:18:57.370 --> 00:19:00.390
The image quality is just enough for my needs,
so I don't need to use it like that.

00:19:00.390 --> 00:19:03.633
Turn it around and just
do it like this,

00:19:03.633 --> 00:19:05.315
I love the big aperture!

00:19:05.333 --> 00:19:06.400
It's a real gem! If
you have no appetite,

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:12.750
this is perfect for supplementing
your diet.

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:14.190
If your teammate has no appetite,

00:19:14.190 --> 00:19:15.910
make him eat this. He just won't
leave because he has no appetite.

00:19:15.910 --> 00:19:18.030
You'll experience a lot of pain,

00:19:18.030 --> 00:19:20.310
so this is considered an essential item
for any pectin jelly tour leader.

00:19:20.310 --> 00:19:22.870
There's something you might need
to save if you don't eat it.

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:24.730
Teammates and leaders! It's
always good to be prepared.

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:26.370
If a teammate doesn't make it,
it might be...

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:28.150
If it costs a lot of money and time,

00:19:28.150 --> 00:19:30.570
the team leader should prepare plenty
of medicine and bandages.

00:19:30.570 --> 00:19:33.030
Don't talk about supplies
and other unnecessary things.

00:19:33.030 --> 00:19:35.050
The explanation "bad
teammate" is better

00:19:35.050 --> 00:19:36.433
interpreted as "not
very good teammate".

00:19:37.250 --> 00:19:38.607
Don't ask your incompetent
teammates

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:44.266
to leave the trailhead in the future.

00:19:45.547 --> 00:19:47.166
Descend the 33.

00:19:47.166 --> 00:19:50.710
3km highway downhill to complete the ascent
of 93 of the 100 highest peaks.

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:53.410
These AKA glasses come
in a new blue square

00:19:53.410 --> 00:19:55.690
color with very light polarization.

00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:57.699
The trip was relatively easy,
so I wore this.

00:19:59.866 --> 00:20:01.769
Around 4.7

00:20:01.799 --> 00:20:03.100
K down 660

00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:03.610
After completing this tower
and mountain pass,

00:20:03.610 --> 00:20:05.750
Hikingbook x UP will be launched.

00:20:05.750 --> 00:20:07.590
Climbing the 100 Great
and Small Peaks,

00:20:07.590 --> 00:20:09.990
with 20 peaks in total,
is easy with 10 of the 100 Great Peaks.

00:20:09.990 --> 00:20:11.590
Among them are the cool badges for
Tower Pass and Mountain Pass,

00:20:11.590 --> 00:20:13.770
and then you collect the
Great Hundred Peaks.

00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:16.010
Completing the Hundred Peaks event
will reward you with special items,

00:20:16.010 --> 00:20:17.390
which I already collected last time.

00:20:17.390 --> 00:20:19.170
Reaching Xiaobaidake is either the
most difficult Xiaobaidake or the

00:20:19.170 --> 00:20:21.230
easiest Dabaidake, depending on whether
it's on Mount Egongji.

00:20:21.230 --> 00:20:23.150
This is very easy. It takes me about
3 hours to go up and down,

00:20:23.150 --> 00:20:25.050
and about an hour at the top.

00:20:25.050 --> 00:20:26.830
It takes three or four hours
to complete a route.

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:29.010
Back in the parking lot,
drive off, dog!

00:20:29.010 --> 00:20:31.190
Oh my god, you yellow
-throated

00:20:31.190 --> 00:20:33.766
weasel!

00:20:41.460 --> 00:20:42.466
The other side of the
Daguanshan Tunnel

00:21:02.960 --> 00:21:06.020
must be packed with cars on weekends.

00:21:06.020 --> 00:21:07.800
So now we need to see where
the trailhead is,

00:21:08.420 --> 00:21:12.920
which is this...

00:21:12.920 --> 00:21:17.780
Next to the tunnel,

00:21:17.780 --> 00:21:20.180
then you have to go around this tunnel,
and now it's foggy.

00:21:20.180 --> 00:21:22.000
It really got foggy,

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:25.620
thankfully we just went to Taguan Mountain
(3176m) and now we're...

00:21:25.620 --> 00:21:28.460
At around 2700 meters,

00:21:28.460 --> 00:21:31.100
the height is roughly around 400 meters. Whether it's
hemlock or spruce isn't important; the key point is...

00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:32.836
This is my 94th Hundred Peaks,

00:21:32.836 --> 00:21:33.420
with 5% remaining.

00:21:33.420 --> 00:21:34.720
After climbing,

00:21:34.720 --> 00:21:36.280
only 5% remains. I've already rambled on too much,
so I won't go into detail.

00:21:36.280 --> 00:21:37.820
Let's get going,

00:21:37.820 --> 00:21:39.600
dog! Just follow this yellow
flag (it's a pole).

00:21:42.833 --> 00:21:43.200
Basically, we're about to walk up

00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:45.699
into the tunnel,
which is pretty cool.

00:21:49.460 --> 00:21:49.910
That static item is

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:52.650
completely dry.

00:21:52.650 --> 00:21:56.450
It's just that this quick
-drying pure wool won't...

00:21:56.450 --> 00:21:57.299
It won't get over
so quickly; actually,

00:22:00.294 --> 00:22:01.890
if you drive a little further,
you'll reach Xiangyang.

00:22:01.890 --> 00:22:03.133
Jiaming Lake is cool,

00:22:06.366 --> 00:22:07.566
all red.

00:22:17.780 --> 00:22:19.633
OSMO has this accessory

00:22:19.633 --> 00:22:21.500
BDS...

00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:24.960
It's just a neck brace,
a very normal thing.

00:22:24.960 --> 00:22:25.799
Please don't get the wrong idea,

00:22:32.422 --> 00:22:33.320
this is just a...

00:22:33.320 --> 00:22:36.133
The boundary is due to the strong

00:22:37.933 --> 00:22:38.220
winds in Yushan National Park.

00:22:38.220 --> 00:22:43.140
I've already climbed over
190 meters up the way.

00:22:43.140 --> 00:22:45.880
There's a thick fog next to me; I've
already started walking from that side.

00:22:45.880 --> 00:22:48.840
The little fox's hiking
shorts came in amidst

00:22:48.840 --> 00:22:52.020
heavy fog but the sun was
still shining brightly.

00:22:52.020 --> 00:22:53.720
It's also breathable and quick
-drying,

00:22:53.720 --> 00:22:55.700
but its elasticity isn't quite as good as it is,
so it won't slip off. So it's not a big difference.

00:22:55.700 --> 00:22:58.140
Walking in this lightweight and quick
-drying

00:22:58.140 --> 00:22:58.766
fabric is very comfortable.

00:23:01.500 --> 00:23:03.245
It's actually quite
easy to climb,

00:23:03.245 --> 00:23:04.060
but the data shows...

00:23:04.060 --> 00:23:06.220
The terrain is rugged
and requires ropes,

00:23:06.220 --> 00:23:07.820
so Wuliaojian is probably
quite dangerous.

00:23:07.820 --> 00:23:08.400
Although I haven't
finished climbing yet,

00:23:08.400 --> 00:23:09.800
I need to be careful about
altitude sickness.

00:23:09.800 --> 00:23:12.540
Don't go up the mountain too late,
or you'll need three or four hours.

00:23:12.540 --> 00:23:15.719
None of these are major problems,
so it's good to look forward to 1994.

00:23:15.733 --> 00:23:19.540
Even on a very high
-class road,

00:23:19.540 --> 00:23:21.460
we didn't find anything,
we didn't find anything at all.

00:23:21.460 --> 00:23:22.300
I just crawled into a
tunnel XD Where's

00:23:22.300 --> 00:23:23.200
my face? Keep it safe.

00:23:23.200 --> 00:23:24.140
Pretty FACE (again,

00:23:24.166 --> 00:23:26.680
in English?) I know some people don't
need to drill through bamboo.

00:23:26.680 --> 00:23:28.960
Saying that couples should film more
movies and go up the mountain

00:23:31.480 --> 00:23:34.620
makes me very sad.
It's not acting; I can't act. @@@@

00:23:34.620 --> 00:23:37.560
The pain is real,

00:23:37.560 --> 00:23:39.940
I never act it out. I also think about it for a long time,
but I'm just prepared.

00:23:39.940 --> 00:23:42.860
You're happy just watching
others suffer?

00:23:42.860 --> 00:23:45.280
You don't torture yourself,
but you...

00:23:45.280 --> 00:23:46.200
It's so unhealthy for
you to enjoy torturing

00:23:46.200 --> 00:23:47.426
others (everyone's sick XD).

00:23:47.466 --> 00:23:50.052
Please take a healthier,
more approachable route.

00:23:50.067 --> 00:23:52.040
You all have to show me,

00:23:52.040 --> 00:23:53.980
okay? I'm forcing you to watch. I'm emphasizing again,
I'm not acting.

00:23:53.980 --> 00:23:56.584
Tired is tired,
relaxed is relaxed, hungry is hungry.

00:23:56.600 --> 00:23:57.533
Handsome is handsome

00:23:59.645 --> 00:24:00.880
(?? New material)

00:24:00.880 --> 00:24:01.533
Is it a new bag? Of course,

00:24:22.360 --> 00:24:24.840
the drawstring terrain won't
cause it to fall off.

00:24:24.840 --> 00:24:26.366
It's safe because
it's on a cliff.

00:24:52.080 --> 00:24:52.866
Guanshanling

00:24:59.299 --> 00:25:01.620
There must be a mysterious

00:25:01.620 --> 00:25:04.999
path leading here.

00:25:08.940 --> 00:25:09.966
Passing through Mobaolai

00:25:13.326 --> 00:25:15.697
and Xitoushan

00:25:16.780 --> 00:25:19.900
The location isn't being
compared to Wuliaojian,

00:25:19.900 --> 00:25:22.140
okay? It's about the
exploration route.

00:25:22.140 --> 00:25:24.000
Hopefully we can go again
sometime in the future.

00:25:24.000 --> 00:25:25.560
Thank you!

00:25:28.333 --> 00:25:29.600
This is my 94th mountain (surprised

00:25:31.783 --> 00:25:32.957
fellow hikers!).

00:25:37.699 --> 00:25:40.160
I'm bringing a headlamp,

00:25:40.160 --> 00:25:42.400
power bank, thermal underwear,
and rain gear with me today. Make sure you bring them!

00:25:44.866 --> 00:25:46.810
Guanshanling Mountain,

00:25:46.833 --> 00:25:49.200
with nothing else to do,
just came here to eat sunflower seeds.

00:25:52.075 --> 00:25:55.860
(How long do you want me to keep
eating sunflower seeds?)

00:25:58.460 --> 00:26:02.300
94. Go down Guanshanling to the Southern Cross
-Island Highway and take a look.

00:26:02.300 --> 00:26:04.640
The Southern Cross
-Island Highway (Southern Cross-Island

00:26:04.640 --> 00:26:06.760
Highway II) is about to be
successfully completed.

00:26:06.760 --> 00:26:08.460
It's not over yet because
the hardest part is driving

00:26:08.460 --> 00:26:11.160
back XD Going down the mountain
will probably be...

00:26:11.160 --> 00:26:13.440
We arrived at the trailhead
around 2 PM

00:26:13.440 --> 00:26:14.066
and set off without further ado, dog!

00:26:32.860 --> 00:26:33.966
The tunnel entrance takes
1 hour and 37 minutes,

00:26:36.240 --> 00:26:38.920
plus a 25
-minute rest at the summit.

00:26:38.920 --> 00:26:41.860
It can be done in about an hour and a half,
so those who are fast...

00:26:41.860 --> 00:26:43.699
It should have taken about an
hour to complete the 93rd

00:26:43.699 --> 00:26:45.400
and 94th peaks of Mount Everest
(I'm so happy!!!!!)

00:26:45.400 --> 00:26:48.400
There are 6 left.

00:26:48.400 --> 00:26:50.500
Which 6? Ma Bo has 4.
Why 4? There's a reason for that (hehe).

00:26:50.500 --> 00:26:54.383
Next are Xuebei and Hehuanxi,
the last one.

00:26:54.400 --> 00:26:55.760
I'll post today's schedule in

00:26:55.760 --> 00:26:57.960
the news section for your reference.

00:26:57.960 --> 00:27:00.220
Then, please note that although it's simple,
you still need to be prepared.

00:27:00.220 --> 00:27:01.833
Going up the mountain is okay.

00:27:01.833 --> 00:27:03.980
The tunnel is a one
-way exit.

00:27:03.980 --> 00:27:04.899
That's all for today's video.

00:27:04.899 --> 00:27:05.233
Did you enjoy my video?

00:27:07.247 --> 00:27:08.000
I'm Hiekr CP.

00:27:08.000 --> 00:27:09.466
See you on the mountain next time!

00:27:09.466 --> 00:27:10.167
Bye
-bye~ Heading back to the trailhead,

00:15:54.334 --> 00:15:56.032
doggy!

00:19:07.729 --> 00:19:08.629
FLOW jelly! Ugh,

00:23:30.372 --> 00:23:31.333
but I don't like it, hahaha.

